---
import { packetExamplePrompt } from '../data/packet-example.mjs';
const { expanded = false } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="packet-example sales-section" aria-labelledby="packet-example-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">A complete free example</p>
  <h2 id="packet-example-title">From “make this better” to a clearer lesson request.</h2>
  <p>Imagine Maple Music, a fictional app for booking music lessons. The school checks availability before confirming a time. The form should make that clear.</p>
  <div class="packet-comparison">
    <figure><figcaption><strong>Before</strong><span>Two actions. An unclear promise.</span></figcaption><div class="packet-screen" role="img" aria-label="Before illustration: a lesson form with unexplained fields and equally prominent Submit and Next actions."><span class="packet-screen-brand">Maple Music</span><h3>Your lesson</h3><div class="sample-field">Email</div><div class="sample-field">Time</div><div class="sample-actions"><span class="sample-button">Submit</span><span class="sample-button">Next</span></div><p>Get started today.</p></div></figure>
    <figure><figcaption><strong>After</strong><span>One action. A clear next step.</span></figcaption><div class="packet-screen" role="img" aria-label="After illustration: the form labels the email and preferred time, offers one Request a lesson action, and explains that availability still needs confirmation."><span class="packet-screen-brand">Maple Music</span><h3>Request your first lesson</h3><span class="sample-label">Email address</span><div class="sample-field">learner@example.com</div><span class="sample-label">Preferred lesson time</span><div class="sample-field">Tuesday, 6:00 pm</div><span class="sample-button sample-button--primary">Request a lesson</span><p>We'll email you to confirm availability. Sending a request doesn't book the lesson yet.</p></div></figure>
  </div>
  <p class="packet-note">These are interface illustrations created for this example. They aren't live booking forms or evidence of a measured sales or usability improvement.</p>
  <div class="packet-reasoning"><h3>What changed, and why?</h3><ol><li><strong>One primary action.</strong> “Request a lesson” describes the task and removes the unexplained second step.</li><li><strong>Labels stay visible.</strong> The learner can still identify each field after entering their details.</li><li><strong>The promise matches the process.</strong> The form explains that a request needs confirmation.</li></ol></div>
  <details class="packet-example-detail" open={expanded}><summary>1. Read and copy the filled-in free prompt</summary><p>This is free prompt 1 with the project, audience, goal, and problem filled in. Add a screenshot of your own screen when you try it.</p><label for="packet-example-prompt">Filled-in screen review</label><textarea id="packet-example-prompt" readonly rows="12" spellcheck="false">{packetExamplePrompt}</textarea><button class="button" type="button" data-copy-packet-prompt>Copy the example prompt</button><p data-packet-copy-status class="packet-note" role="status"></p><p><a href="/builder?prompt=1">Customize the same free prompt for your screen →</a></p></details>
  <details class="packet-example-detail" open={expanded}><summary>2. Compare the answer with a useful review</summary><p class="packet-note">The review below was written for this demonstration. AI answers vary; this isn't a recorded customer result.</p><ul><li><strong>Must fix:</strong> explain that the form requests a time rather than confirming a booking.</li><li><strong>Should improve:</strong> keep field labels visible and use one clearly named primary action.</li><li><strong>Keep:</strong> the existing fields and request process. There's no need to add an account, payment screen, or new feature.</li></ul><p>A useful follow-up is: “Apply only those form changes. Keep the existing request handler. Explain how to check that errors and confirmation still work.”</p></details>
  <details class="packet-example-detail" open={expanded}><summary>3. Check your own result</summary><p>Mark these only after checking a real screen you've changed. These boxes record your review; they don't run tests.</p><label class="packet-check"><input type="checkbox"/>The main button describes what actually happens.</label><label class="packet-check"><input type="checkbox"/>An invalid email shows a useful error without clearing other entries.</label><label class="packet-check"><input type="checkbox"/>I can complete the form with a keyboard and read it on a phone.</label><label class="packet-check"><input type="checkbox"/>A successful request shows the correct next step and doesn't create a duplicate.</label></details>
</section>
